+# The recorded Preimage Fibre changes the continuing temporal response
+
+**Date:** September 7, 2026. **Branch:** `codex/apple-silicon`.
+
+[project-postulate] Brandon's resumed AS4–AS5 goal requires useful sound perception/production,
+then useful recorded English/conversation, with continuing application, persistence, streaming
+and measured consumer costs. This return advances the recorded condition contact. It does not
+complete the acoustic product or change the independent desktop cultivation direction.
+
+## Construction and actual scope
+
+[definition] For the retained source convolution restricted to actual observed support S, write
+`X=R_S X_x`. The complete compatible family is `F_y={(h,e): Xh+e=y}`. Every response direction
+remains available with its correlated unexplained return. The declared unit-admittance contact
+uses `A=I+X*X`, `U=A^-1 X*y`, `V=A^-1 h_0` and returns:
+
+- Successor joint current: `(U+V, y-X(U+V))`.
+- Incoming normal: `(U, y-XU)`.
+- Returned normal: `(h_0-V, XV)`.
+- Joint difference: `(U+V-h_0, y-X(U+V))`.
+
+[definition] This is the existing two-port projection law on the structured temporal graph.
+The returned normal belongs to `ker[X I]`'s orthogonal complement; it is not asserted to be a
+point of `F_y`. The metric is explicit. No unique physical cause or zero unexplained current is
+inferred. Outside-S coefficients remain retained operands rather than zero observations.
+
+[established-bounded; source-inspected] The dense bilinear preimage owner could not express
+this arbitrary temporal graph without expanding the full recording into a dense relation.
+`constitutive_fibre/resident/condition_contact/temporal.rs` supplies its structured representation
+under the existing contact owner. It retains the actual producing convolution/comparison and
+immutable producing cut; later evidence contacts the current successor without rewriting that
+prediction. Fresh reports and all normal/unexplained waveform legs must return before atomic
+publication. The continuing ecology has one move owner.
+
+[established-bounded; source-inspected] CUDA and Metal share the declared Gram/RHS construction,
+the extracted existing LDL factorization and exact residual certification from `A>=I`.
+Dyadic centres and global Euclidean radii remain native numerical enclosures. The new enclosed
+phase consumer carries them through full convolution and comparison without exposing a point
+current from a centre. Directed integer rounding and source/product error contribute to the
+complete waveform bound. The exact initial section and successive integer Gram/cross moments
+remain sufficient for a separate cold rational decoder of the response. Contact receipts retain
+the larger recording-relative fibre; the continuing response does not require a raw-wave archive.
+
+## Verification and recorded continuation
+
+[established-bounded; measured] Four native contact controls, 29 temporal-current checks and
+three field-solver regressions pass on Apple M1 Pro. They cover complex/non-dyadic currents,
+the full convolution tail, structural padding distinct from excluded observations, plural
+compatible pairs, exact two-port energy and normal equations, stale producing cuts, foreign
+owners, equal-but-different predictions and arithmetic refusal preserving the predecessor.
+The existing public internal-mode example also passes; its 391-byte output matches the prior
+desktop/Apple artifact byte for byte. No Lean source changed. CUDA was source-inspected here;
+these are Metal execution measurements, not a new CUDA execution claim.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] `recorded_acoustic_contact` conducts all three original 14-second
+SoundCam electrical-loopback/microphone-0 pairs at 48 kHz, in row order 0,1,2. Each prediction
+precedes native reception of that pair's microphone section, and its contact changes the response
+used by the next recording. The declared aperture is four complex taps at the original sample
+step, starting from the explicit unit impulse; the numerical grain is 72. These are experimental
+chart/representation declarations, not learned semantic grains or a calibrated room response.
+All 672,000 observed frames participate; the three prediction-tail frames remain unobserved.
+
+| Pair | Prediction (s) | Comparison (s) | Complete contact (s) | Three native stages (s) |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Row 0 | 4.372 | 4.090 | 27.266 | 35.729 |
+| Row 1 | 4.442 | 4.044 | 27.299 | 35.784 |
+| Row 2 | 4.286 | 4.103 | 27.493 | 35.881 |
+
+[established-bounded; measured] Each complete contact uses six resident deeds, 36 allocations,
+zero numerical ingress/readout and 384 bytes of receipt egress. The entire driver takes
+115.245881 seconds for 42 seconds of source material, including codec and declared cold evidence
+work. Peak native residency is 392,470,932 bytes. After waveform receipts leave scope, the
+continuing response and its retained constructions occupy 14,544 native bytes. Each portable
+contact section is 4,744 bytes. Cold evidence exports occur between records in this experiment;
+they do not feed a native current. This is not a real-time, power or energy measurement.
+
+[established-bounded; measured] The independent Python observer verifies the original NPY
+selectors against WAV hashes/bytes, every retained Gram/cross moment and solve residual, the
+exact recursive response and all waveform/current balls using the **sum** of squared errors
+against the global radius. It uses integer common-denominator arrays and exact rationals,
+without binary floating-point complex arithmetic or tolerances. All three comparisons pass.
+Six negative observer controls reject an exceeded joint radius, unequal W endpoints, a changed
+solve residual despite a matching checksum, a wrong clock, altered chronology and a claimed hot
+readout. Two positive controls preserve signed-128 limb boundaries and non-dyadic arithmetic.
+
+## Evidence and continuation
+
+[definition] The [portable evidence](2026-09-07_recorded_temporal_condition_contact/) contains
+the actual return/comparison, observer-control outcomes and three small contact sections.
+Full waveform sections remain at `.local/experiments/soundcam-native-temporal-contact/sections`;
+source recordings remain in `.local/datasets/soundcam`. The public commands are in the
+[acoustic guide](../../docs/ACOUSTIC_EXPERIMENTS.md). The source-qualified observer is
+`research/experiments/apple_silicon/compare_recorded_acoustic_contact.py`.
+
+[definition] Observer controls call its public verification helpers. The joint-radius control
+uses two real coordinates `3/4` against zero with global radius 1. The signed-wire control
+round-trips `-1`, `2^63`, `-2^63` and `2^100+11`. The residual control changes both endpoint
+words of the first U-residual coordinate and recomputes the section checksum. Clock, chronology
+and census controls change their corresponding actual report fields. Their recoverable local
+fixtures are in the experiment's `observer-controls` directory.
+
+[open] Next persist/remount this continuing response with its exact construction, bind enclosed
+temporal emissions to the declared acoustic codec/receiver, and develop useful sound conduct
+through actual material and conditions. The four-tap study does not establish a sound model,
+speech recognition/generation, English usefulness, streaming completion or AS4–AS5 completion.
